 "amended": "28 October 2026, after the first fit and its benchmark: the second takes were dev (and sealed at F#1, E4 and G#5), but 126 of the 143 share their first take's hammer impact noise, which differs from strike to strike, and nine in ten of those sit under 0.15 cents from it (the median over their first six partials): the first take played back a fraction of a cent off and a few samples later (Tools/find_repeated_takes.py). All but F#1's softest correlate with their first take at 0.96 or more over the first half second, so none can hold out what the first takes calibrate. Every second take became 'repeat'; train is unchanged.",
 "rules": {
  "train": "every layer's first take at the 28 recorded pitches other than those below, with their release takes and hammer noises",
  "dev": "every first take at D#2, G#3, C5 and E6 (MIDI 39, 56, 72, 88) and B3's single take (MIDI 59, top layer only): scored at every iteration and used to choose between candidates, never fitted",
  "sealed": "every first take at F#1, E4 and G#5 (MIDI 30, 64, 80): opened only to report a candidate the owner is asked to approve, each opening recorded",
  "repeat": "every second take: neither fitted nor scored, as it repeats the strike its first take holds"
 },
